---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
  caption="Selected pathways from POMC. PC1/3 releases ACTH. In tissues with PC2, ACTH can be processed further to yield α-MSH, which signals through receptors including MC1R and MC4R."
  source="Harno et al. · Physiological Reviews (2018)"
>
  <svg class="schematic" viewBox="0 0 400 265" role="img" aria-label="POMC processing and three melanocortin receptor pathways">
    <desc>PC1/3 processing of POMC releases ACTH. ACTH activates MC2R to stimulate cortisol production. In tissues with PC2, further processing of ACTH yields α-MSH, which can act through MC1R in pigmentation and MC4R in appetite regulation.</desc>

    <rect class="node" x="20" y="16" width="112" height="37" />
    <text x="76" y="41">POMC</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M76 53 V96 m-5-5 5 5 5-5" />
    <text class="detail" x="121" y="80">PC1/3</text>

    <rect class="active-node" x="20" y="104" width="112" height="40" />
    <text x="76" y="130">ACTH</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M132 124 H216 m-5-5 5 5-5 5" />
    <text class="detail" x="174" y="111">via PC2</text>
    <rect class="active-node" x="224" y="104" width="112" height="40" />
    <text x="280" y="130">α-MSH</text>

    <path class="flow" d="M76 144 V192 m-5-5 5 5 5-5 M280 144 V167 H200 V192 m-5-5 5 5 5-5 M280 167 H324 V192 m-5-5 5 5 5-5" />

    <rect class="node" x="20" y="200" width="112" height="49" />
    <rect class="node" x="144" y="200" width="112" height="49" />
    <rect class="node" x="268" y="200" width="112" height="49" />
    <text x="76" y="220">MC2R<tspan class="detail" x="76" dy="21">Cortisol</tspan></text>
    <text x="200" y="220">MC1R<tspan class="detail" x="200" dy="21">Pigmentation</tspan></text>
    <text x="324" y="220">MC4R<tspan class="detail" x="324" dy="21">Appetite</tspan></text>
  </svg>
</Figure>
